//? Title: K-Means: Tensor Distortion and SGD Restarts
//? Subtitle: Cluster IDs are arbitrary; compare distances and centres
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Unlabelled points can be compressed into nearby representative centres, but different starts
can produce different partitions. We cluster a six-point line whose two centroids are known,
verify tensor distortion from assignments, and compare restart budgets on a fixed cloud.
No class labels enter the fit.
)
\toc

> The method

For observations X and centres C, minimise the mean nearest-centre distortion

$$
J(C)=\frac1N\sum_i\min_k\|x_i-c_k\|^2,\qquad
\nabla_{c_k}J=\frac2N\sum_{i:a_i=k}(c_k-x_i).
$$
\alttext(The mean nearest-centre squared error differentiates through the active cluster assignment.)

Away from distance ties, assignments are locally constant, so ordinary tensor autograd gives
the displayed gradient. The explicit SGD loop updates centres at rate .3. For fixed assignments,
its update moves each centre towards its assigned mean; Lloyd's exact mean update is a different
algorithm. A tie is nondifferentiable, and an empty cluster has zero gradient. Restarts reduce
initialisation sensitivity. Retain the smallest final objective from the same seeded sequence
of starts; extending that sequence cannot worsen its best value. Each step costs O(NKD) and
materialises [N,K,D] differences. The plotted cloud shows every generated input observation.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/kmeans_clustering_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/kmeans_clustering_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/kmeans_clustering_concept.tikz > build/kmeans_clustering_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/kmeans_clustering_concept.svg build/kmeans_clustering_concept.dvi > build/kmeans_clustering_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/kmeans_clustering_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
